-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Aspects of quality of life in haemodialysis patients</article-title><source>Journal of American Society of Nephrology</source><year>1996</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>1418</fpage><lpage>26</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gokal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quality of life in patients undergoing renal replacement therapy</article-title><source>Kidney International</source><year>1993</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>23</fpage><lpage>7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Christensen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ehlers</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychological Factors in End &#x02013; Stage Renal Disease: An Emerging Context for Behavioral Medicine Research</article-title><source>Journal of Consulting and Clinical Psychology</source><year>2002</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>712</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12090378</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0022-006X.70.3.712</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Griffin</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Khanna R</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of quality of life in haemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis patients</article-title><source>Advances in peritoneal dialysis</source><year>1994</year><publisher-name>Toronto: Peritoneal Dialysis Publications</publisher-name><fpage>104</fpage><lpage>08</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7999804</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><su